  "name": "FREE PSA:TOTAL PSA RATIO",
  "code": " PSA ",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Test Usage:</strong></p><p>The percentage of measured PSA existing in the free form (free:total PSA ratio) is useful in assessing the risk of prostate cancer in patients with borderline or moderately increased total PSA (4-10 ng/mL).</p><p><strong>Reference Range:</strong></p><p>When total PSA is in the range of 4.0-10.0 ng/mL, a free:total PSA ratio &lt; or =0.10 indicates 49% to 65% risk of prostate cancer depending on age; a free:total PSA ratio &gt;0.25 indicates a 9% to 16% risk of prostate cancer, depending on age.</p>",
